We have hit an architectural ceiling with flat sequence modeling. Stacking more layers and widening attention heads is the brute-force answer to a geometric problem: we are trying to map complex, multi-scale relational data onto low-dimensional spatial grids, and then wondering why models hallucinate, drift, or forget structural context over long horizons.
If you want a cognitive loop that doesn't bloat your hardware footprint, you have to change the geometry of how tokens interact. You have to move from flat matrices to E8 root lattices and 4D attention manifolds.
